<section class="content-section product-detail-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">BUYER'S GUIDE</p><h2>Choosing attendance software for your team</h2><p>Attendance software should make daily records easier to collect and review without creating a burdensome process for employees or managers. Before rollout, decide how staff will check in, which verification methods are necessary, how exceptions are handled and who can view reports.</p></div><div class="page-grid"><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">01</span><h3>QR-based check-in and check-out</h3><p>Review the check-in journey, employee onboarding and what happens when a device or network is unavailable.</p></article>
<article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">02</span><h3>Verification and privacy</h3><p>Confirm whether GPS and photo verification are enabled for your plan and location, define access rules and explain the process to employees.</p></article>
<article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">03</span><h3>Shifts and attendance reporting</h3><p>List the schedules, late-arrival rules, summaries and exports managers need before selecting a configuration.</p></article></div></div></section>
